+# replay plus guide
+
+## installing
+
+easiest way is the updater. grab `ReplayPlusUpdater.exe` from the
+[releases page](https://github.com/vraxa/replay-plus/releases/latest), close skate. and the reskate launcher, and
+run it. the first time it asks where your ReSkateLauncher.exe is, then just hit Install.
+
+it downloads the newest replay plus and the reskate launcher that goes with it (from reskate's own releases),
+checks every file before it touches anything, keeps a copy of what you had, and turns off the launcher's auto
+updates so it doesn't swap the dll back. run it again whenever you want to update. "Remove Replay Plus" swaps it
+back to the plain animator studio (the same version, from fourth studio's own release) and keeps your presets, and
+"Put back what I had before" undoes the lot. if you're not running replay plus, "Update Animator Studio" keeps the
+plain studio up to date (with the reskate launcher it goes with), or gets it for you on plain reskate.
+
+on mac and linux the game runs through crossover, whisky, proton or wine, so reskate lives inside that bottle or
+prefix (its drive_c). there's an updater for those too, in the same release:
+
+- mac (apple silicon): `ReplayPlusUpdater-macOS.zip`. unzip it and open Replay Plus Updater. macOS blocks it the
+  first time since it isn't from the app store, so go to System Settings > Privacy & Security and hit Open Anyway
+- linux: `ReplayPlusUpdater-x86_64.AppImage`. make it executable (`chmod +x`, or right click > properties > allow
+  running it as a program) and open it
+
+they look for your reskate folder in the usual bottles and prefixes on their own, or you can point them at it (on
+mac, Cmd+Shift+. shows hidden folders like Library).
+
+doing it by hand: rename your ReSkate.dll to ReSkate.dll.studio, put the new one in, and set `"updates"` to
+`false` in ReSkateLauncher.settings.json.
+
+## the menu
+
+in the replay editor hold R3 and press RB, or press F10.
+
+- LB / RB: tabs
+- dpad: up and down picks a row, left and right changes it (hold to go faster)
+- A selects, X resets to default, holding Y hides the menu so you can see the picture, B closes it
+
+on keyboard it's the arrows, Enter, R, Q / E and Backspace. you can still scrub the replay with the triggers
+while the menu's open.
+
+## R3 shortcuts
+
+hold R3 in the replay editor and:
+
+- RB: open the menu
+- dpad up / down: focus further / nearer (puts a focus key where you are)
+- LT / RT: less / more blur
+- dpad right: a focus key here
+- dpad left: shake on / off
+- LB: a shake key (turns the shake on or off from that point)
+- View: delete the keys where you are
+
+F10 opens the menu and F11 turns the shake on or off. focus keys show up blue and shake keys orange on the
+timeline. a quick tap of R3 is still the game's photo button.
+
+## the tabs
+
+- shake: handheld shake, its style, strength and speed
+- lens: the fisheye. distortion (0% is no lens at all), image circle, edge squish, zoom and squeeze, plus fringe,
+  shade, glare and softness if you want it to look like cheap glass. the field of view can be the editor's own,
+  fixed, or auto
+- frame: 4:3 or 2.39 bars, and an overlay, either your own png (a lens hood or whatever) or a round edge
+- colour: a camcorder curve, exposure, contrast, saturation, warmth, lift / gamma / gain, split toning, grain
+  and vignette
+- focus: depth of field, fixed, keyframed along the replay, or auto. it blurs what's behind the focus too
+- light: a light on the camera
+- game: the game's own effects held where you put them (motion blur, bloom, lens flares, fog, exposure and so on)
+- video: sharp middle (renders finer so a wide fisheye doesn't go soft in the middle), the editor's picture shape
+  (a real 4:3 that isn't stretched), render resolutions, and a bigger texture pool for big maps
+- presets: your saved looks
+
+## presets
+
+Save as new saves everything as it is and asks for a name. on a preset, left / right picks what A does: load,
+rename, export or delete (delete asks twice and it goes to the recycle bin).
+
+export puts a copy in the export folder, that's the file you send people. presets people send you go in the import
+folder and get added on their own after a few seconds.
+
+there are two to start from, Fisheye 16-9 and Fisheye 4-3. if you delete them they stay deleted.
+
+## where stuff is
+
+| what | where |
+|---|---|
+| presets | `%LOCALAPPDATA%\ReSkate\Replay Plus\Presets` |
+| presets people send you | `%LOCALAPPDATA%\ReSkate\Replay Plus\Import` |
+| presets you export | `%LOCALAPPDATA%\ReSkate\Replay Plus\Export` |
+| overlay pngs | `%LOCALAPPDATA%\ReSkate\Replay Plus\Overlays` |
+| settings | `%LOCALAPPDATA%\ReSkate\profiles\offline\replay_plus.json` |
+
+## good to know
+
+- everything shows up in exported videos too, not just on screen
+- for sharper exports turn up Export quality in Insert > SETTINGS > REPLAYS
+- the 4:3 picture shape needs the game in borderless fullscreen (that's the default)
+- the R3 shortcuts need an xinput controller, so an xbox pad, or a ps pad through ds4windows or steam input
+- the studio's own updater is off in this dll since it would put back a studio without replay plus. use the
+  replay plus updater instead
+- `replayplus help` in the console (~) lists every command
diff --git a/Extension/ReplayPlus/ReplayPlus.cmake b/Extension/ReplayPlus/ReplayPlus.cmake
new file mode 100644
index 00000000..f3751c1a
--- /dev/null
+++ b/Extension/ReplayPlus/ReplayPlus.cmake
@@ -0,0 +1,98 @@
+# Replay Plus (README.md), added to ReSkate's targets by Extension/ReplayShake/ReplayShake.cmake, which
+# includes this file once Replay Shake's own model library is defined.
+
+# The picture pass's shader is built into the DLL as text and compiled when it is first drawn (as
+# ReSkate's screen look is, cmake/UI.cmake); the build checks it with the Windows SDK's fxc when there
+# is one, so a shader that would not compile in the game fails here instead.
+set(replay_plus_hlsl_path "${PROJECT_SOURCE_DIR}/Extension/ReplayPlus/replay_plus.hlsl")
+set_property(DIRECTORY APPEND PROPERTY CMAKE_CONFIGURE_DEPENDS "${replay_plus_hlsl_path}")
+file(READ "${replay_plus_hlsl_path}" replay_plus_hlsl_source)
+# MSVC takes at most about 16 KB in one string literal: the shader goes in as several, which the
+# compiler joins.
+string(LENGTH "${replay_plus_hlsl_source}" replay_plus_hlsl_length)
+set(replay_plus_hlsl_chunks "")
+set(replay_plus_hlsl_at 0)
+while(replay_plus_hlsl_at LESS replay_plus_hlsl_length)
+    string(SUBSTRING "${replay_plus_hlsl_source}" ${replay_plus_hlsl_at} 8000 replay_plus_hlsl_chunk)
+    string(APPEND replay_plus_hlsl_chunks "R\"replay_plus_hlsl(${replay_plus_hlsl_chunk})replay_plus_hlsl\"\n")
+    math(EXPR replay_plus_hlsl_at "${replay_plus_hlsl_at} + 8000")
+endwhile()
+file(CONFIGURE OUTPUT "${CMAKE_CURRENT_BINARY_DIR}/generated/replay_plus_hlsl.h" @ONLY CONTENT
+"#pragma once
+// Generated by Extension/ReplayPlus/ReplayPlus.cmake from Extension/ReplayPlus/replay_plus.hlsl.
+inline constexpr const char* replay_plus_hlsl =
+@replay_plus_hlsl_chunks@;
+")
+if(WIN32)
+    if(NOT DINGOSDK_FXC)
+        file(GLOB replay_plus_fxc_candidates "C:/Program Files (x86)/Windows Kits/10/bin/10.*/x64/fxc.exe")
+        if(replay_plus_fxc_candidates)
+            list(SORT replay_plus_fxc_candidates)
+            list(REVERSE replay_plus_fxc_candidates)
+            list(GET replay_plus_fxc_candidates 0 replay_plus_fxc)
+        endif()
+    else()
+        set(replay_plus_fxc "${DINGOSDK_FXC}")
+    endif()
+    if(replay_plus_fxc)
+        set(replay_plus_checked "${CMAKE_CURRENT_BINARY_DIR}/generated/replay_plus.checked")
+        add_custom_command(OUTPUT "${replay_plus_checked}"
+            COMMAND "${replay_plus_fxc}" /nologo /T vs_5_0 /E vs_main /Fo "${CMAKE_CURRENT_BINARY_DIR}/generated/replay_plus_vs.cso" "${replay_plus_hlsl_path}"
+            COMMAND "${replay_plus_fxc}" /nologo /T ps_5_0 /E ps_decode /Fo "${CMAKE_CURRENT_BINARY_DIR}/generated/replay_plus_decode.cso" "${replay_plus_hlsl_path}"
+            COMMAND "${replay_plus_fxc}" /nologo /T ps_5_0 /E ps_down /Fo "${CMAKE_CURRENT_BINARY_DIR}/generated/replay_plus_down.cso" "${replay_plus_hlsl_path}"
+            COMMAND "${replay_plus_fxc}" /nologo /T ps_5_0 /E ps_main /Fo "${CMAKE_CURRENT_BINARY_DIR}/generated/replay_plus_main.cso" "${replay_plus_hlsl_path}"
+            COMMAND "${CMAKE_COMMAND}" -E touch "${replay_plus_checked}"
+            DEPENDS "${replay_plus_hlsl_path}"
+            COMMENT "Checking Replay Plus's shader with fxc"
+            VERBATIM)
+        add_custom_target(dingosdk_replay_plus_shader_check DEPENDS "${replay_plus_checked}")
+    endif()
+endif()
+
+# Its settings, presets, lens maths and the hand-overs between its sides: no game access, shared by the
+# runtime, the overlay and the tests.
+add_library(dingosdk_replay_plus_model STATIC
+    Extension/ReplayPlus/replay_plus_settings.cpp
+    Extension/ReplayPlus/replay_plus_lens.cpp
+    Extension/ReplayPlus/replay_plus_link.cpp)
+target_include_directories(dingosdk_replay_plus_model PUBLIC "${PROJECT_SOURCE_DIR}")
+target_link_libraries(dingosdk_replay_plus_model PUBLIC dingosdk_json dingosdk_replay_shake_model)
+
+# Test builds only: console lines dropped into a folder's inbox.txt are run in the game, one a tick,
+# their answers written to outbox.txt beside it (replay_plus.cpp run_inbox). Releases leave it off.
+option(DINGOSDK_REPLAY_PLUS_TEST_INBOX "Replay Plus: run console lines from a test folder's inbox.txt (testing only)" OFF)
+set(DINGOSDK_REPLAY_PLUS_TEST_FOLDER "${CMAKE_BINARY_DIR}/replay-plus-test" CACHE PATH "Replay Plus: the test inbox's folder")
+
+if(TARGET dingosdk_runtime)
+    target_sources(dingosdk_runtime PRIVATE Extension/ReplayPlus/replay_plus.cpp Extension/ReplayPlus/replay_plus_window.cpp)
+    set_property(SOURCE Extension/ReplayPlus/replay_plus.cpp APPEND PROPERTY INCLUDE_DIRECTORIES "${CMAKE_CURRENT_BINARY_DIR}/generated")
+    target_link_libraries(dingosdk_runtime PRIVATE dingosdk_replay_plus_model windowscodecs ole32)
+    if(DINGOSDK_REPLAY_PLUS_TEST_INBOX)
+        set_property(SOURCE Extension/ReplayPlus/replay_plus.cpp APPEND PROPERTY COMPILE_DEFINITIONS
+            "REPLAY_PLUS_TEST_INBOX=\"${DINGOSDK_REPLAY_PLUS_TEST_FOLDER}\"")
+        # The panel reads ReSkate's scripted pad too (the test inbox's `replayplus pad`).
+        set_property(SOURCE Extension/ReplayPlus/replay_plus_panel.cpp APPEND PROPERTY COMPILE_DEFINITIONS REPLAY_PLUS_TEST_PAD=1)
+    endif()
+endif()
+if(TARGET dingosdk_overlay)
+    target_sources(dingosdk_overlay PRIVATE
+        Extension/ReplayPlus/replay_plus_render.cpp
+        Extension/ReplayPlus/replay_plus_depth.cpp
+        Extension/ReplayPlus/replay_plus_panel.cpp)
+    target_include_directories(dingosdk_overlay PRIVATE "${CMAKE_CURRENT_BINARY_DIR}/generated")
+    target_link_libraries(dingosdk_overlay PUBLIC dingosdk_replay_plus_model PRIVATE d3d12 d3dcompiler)
+    if(TARGET dingosdk_replay_plus_shader_check)
+        add_dependencies(dingosdk_overlay dingosdk_replay_plus_shader_check)
+    endif()
+endif()
+
+option(DINGOSDK_BUILD_REPLAY_PLUS_TESTS "Build Replay Plus regression tests" OFF)
+# With Replay Shake's too (update-reskate.ps1 builds those, and runs both).
+if(DINGOSDK_BUILD_REPLAY_PLUS_TESTS OR DINGOSDK_BUILD_REPLAY_SHAKE_TESTS)
+    enable_testing()
+    # Its settings and verbs, presets and share codes, and the lens: no game and no Windows.
+    add_executable(dingosdk_replay_plus_tests Extension/ReplayPlus/Test/replay_plus_tests.cpp)
+    target_include_directories(dingosdk_replay_plus_tests PRIVATE "${PROJECT_SOURCE_DIR}")
+    target_link_libraries(dingosdk_replay_plus_tests PRIVATE dingosdk_replay_plus_model)
+    add_test(NAME replay_plus COMMAND dingosdk_replay_plus_tests)
+endif()
diff --git a/Extension/ReplayPlus/Test/replay_plus_tests.cpp b/Extension/ReplayPlus/Test/replay_plus_tests.cpp
new file mode 100644
index 00000000..464550ed
--- /dev/null
+++ b/Extension/ReplayPlus/Test/replay_plus_tests.cpp
@@ -0,0 +1,1132 @@
+// Replay Plus with no game: every value's table entry, the `replayplus` verbs, the saved settings (and those saved
+// before the lens was settings only), presets and their names, the lens (against its reference
+// numbers) and its edge compression, the overlay's picture, the grade, and an exported frame
+// finished on the CPU.
+#include "Extension/ReplayPlus/replay_plus_lens.h"
+#include "Extension/ReplayPlus/replay_plus_settings.h"
+#include "Extension/ReplayShake/replay_shake_model.h"
+#include <algorithm>
+#include <array>
+#include <cmath>
+#include <cstdio>
+#include <format>
+#include <set>
+#include <functional>
+#include <iostream>
+#include <random>
+#include <stdexcept>
+#include <string>
+#include <vector>
+
+using namespace dingosdk;
+using namespace dingosdk::replay_plus;
+void migration_tests();
+void camera_curve_tests();
+namespace {
+void fit_is_tight(const lens::Frame& f, const std::string& what);
+int checks = 0;
+void check(bool value, const std::string& message) {
+    ++checks;
+    if (!value) throw std::runtime_error(message);
+}
+bool near(double a, double b, double tolerance = 1e-4) { return std::abs(a - b) <= tolerance; }
+using Words = std::vector<std::string>;
+Reply run(Settings& settings, const std::string& verb, const Words& words) { return command(settings, verb, words); }
+float radians(float degrees) { return degrees * lens::pi / 180.0f; }
+
+// A lens hood picture of the tests' own: 4:3, black outside an ellipse (an adapter's image circle, 1.54
+// half-heights, stretched with its overlay across the window: 1.1294 by 1.54 in the picture's own units), so its
+// black shows in the corners only; measured as Replay Plus measures a picture.
+lens::Hole hood_hole() {
+    static const lens::Hole hole = [] {
+        const std::uint32_t w = 1440, h = 1080;
+        std::vector<std::uint8_t> rgba(std::size_t{w} * h * 4, 0);
+        for (std::uint32_t y = 0; y < h; ++y)
+            for (std::uint32_t x = 0; x < w; ++x) {
+                const float u = (static_cast<float>(x) + 0.5f) / static_cast<float>(w) * 2 - 1, v = 1 - (static_cast<float>(y) + 0.5f) / static_cast<float>(h) * 2;
+                rgba[(std::size_t{y} * w + x) * 4 + 3] = (u / 1.1294f) * (u / 1.1294f) + (v / 1.54f) * (v / 1.54f) >= 1 ? 255 : 0;
+            }
+        return lens::measure_hole(rgba.data(), w, h);
+    }();
+    return hole;
+}
+// The angle off-axis (radians) a point of the game's picture looks along.
+double angle_in_game(const lens::Frame& f, std::array<float, 2> uv) {
+    const auto tg = lens::tangents(f);
+    const double x = (uv[0] - 0.5) * 2.0 * tg[0], y = (0.5 - uv[1]) * 2.0 * tg[1];
+    return std::atan(std::sqrt(x * x + y * y));
+}
+// The direction (unit) a point of a game's picture looks along, at its field of view and aspect.
+std::array<double, 3> direction_in_game(double u, double v, double fov, double aspect) {
+    const double ty = std::tan(fov * 0.5), tx = ty * aspect;
+    const double x = (u * 2 - 1) * tx, y = (1 - v * 2) * ty, n = std::sqrt(x * x + y * y + 1);
+    return {x / n, y / n, 1 / n};
+}
+double between_directions(const std::array<double, 3>& a, const std::array<double, 3>& b) {
+    const double cx = a[1] * b[2] - a[2] * b[1], cy = a[2] * b[0] - a[0] * b[2], cz = a[0] * b[1] - a[1] * b[0];
+    return std::atan2(std::sqrt(cx * cx + cy * cy + cz * cz), a[0] * b[0] + a[1] * b[1] + a[2] * b[2]);
+}
+const Preset& built_in(const std::string& name) {
+    static const auto list = built_in_presets();
+    for (const auto& p : list)
+        if (p.name == name) return p;
+    throw std::runtime_error("no built-in preset " + name);
+}
+
+void field_tests() {
+    const Settings defaults;
+    std::set<std::string_view> keys;
+    for (const auto& f : fields()) {
+        check(keys.insert(f.key).second, std::string("one field per key: ") + std::string(f.key));
+        check(f.get && f.set, std::string(f.key) + " reads and writes");
+        const float v = f.get(defaults);
+        if (f.kind == Kind::number) check(v >= f.low && v <= f.high, std::string(f.key) + "'s default is within its range");
+        if (f.kind == Kind::choice) check(f.choices.size() == f.labels.size() && v >= 0 && v < static_cast<float>(f.choices.size()),
+                                          std::string(f.key) + "'s choices have labels, and its default is one");
+        // Shown and read back, every step of the way: what the panel shows, `set` takes.
+        Settings s;
+        const int steps = f.kind == Kind::number ? static_cast<int>(std::round((f.high - f.low) / f.step)) : static_cast<int>(f.choices.size()) + 1;
+        for (int i = 0; i <= std::min(steps, 400); ++i) {
+            if (f.kind == Kind::number) f.set(s, std::min(f.high, f.low + static_cast<float>(i) * f.step));
+            else step(f, s, 1);
+            const float before = f.get(s);
+            Settings t = defaults;
+            std::string why;
+            check(assign(f, t, shown(f, s), why), std::string(f.key) + " takes back what it shows: " + shown(f, s) + " " + why);
+            float tolerance = f.kind == Kind::number ? f.step * 0.51f + 1e-4f : 0.0f;
+            if (f.logarithmic) tolerance = (before < 1 ? 0.005f : before < 10 ? 0.05f : 0.5f) + 1e-4f; // two figures shown
+            check(std::abs(f.get(t) - before) <= tolerance, std::string(f.key) + " reads back as it was shown: " + shown(f, s));
+        }
+        // Stepping stays within the range; choices wrap.
+        Settings u;
+        step(f, u, 10000);
+        check(f.kind != Kind::number || f.get(u) <= f.high, std::string(f.key) + " steps up to its top");
+        step(f, u, -20000);
+        check(f.kind != Kind::number || f.get(u) >= f.low, std::string(f.key) + " steps down to its bottom");
+    }
+    check(field("lens.zoom") && field("LENS.ZOOM") && !field("lens.nothing"), "fields are found by key, in any case");
+    // Numbers in the panel's units or kept ones.
+    Settings s;
+    std::string why;
+    check(assign(*field("video.replay"), s, "150%", why) && near(s.replay_scale, 1.5), "150% is 1.5");
+    check(assign(*field("video.replay"), s, "175", why) && near(s.replay_scale, 1.75), "a number in the shown units is taken as shown");
+    check(assign(*field("video.replay"), s, "1.25", why) && near(s.replay_scale, 1.25), "a kept number is taken as kept");
+    check(assign(*field("video.replay"), s, "9", why) && near(s.replay_scale, 2.0), "past the top is the top");
+    check(!assign(*field("video.replay"), s, "lots", why), "words are not numbers");
+    check(assign(*field("frame.hood"), s, "Picture", why) && s.hood == Hood::picture, "a choice by its label");
+    check(assign(*field("frame.hood"), s, "circle", why) && s.hood == Hood::circle, "a choice by its name");
+    check(!assign(*field("frame.hood"), s, "zoom lens", why), "a choice that is not one");
+    check(!field("lens.mode") && !field("lens.true") && !field("grade.camcorder"), "no switch between looks: the lens is its settings");
+    check(assign(*field("light.on"), s, "on", why) && s.light && assign(*field("light.on"), s, "toggle", why) && !s.light, "toggles");
+    check(assign(*field("fov.degrees"), s, "150°", why) && near(s.fov, 150), "a unit after the number");
+    // Relevance: a value that does nothing as things are is shown locked.
+    Settings r;
+    check(!field("lens.circle")->relevant(r), "no distortion: no image circle");
+    r.curve = 1;
+    check(field("lens.circle")->relevant(r) && !field("lens.zoom")->relevant, "a fisheye's circle; the zoom always counts");
+    check(!field("frame.opacity")->relevant(r), "no overlay: no opacity");
+    r.hood = Hood::picture;
+    check(field("frame.opacity")->relevant(r), "an overlay's opacity");
+    check(!field("grade.camera_gamma")->relevant(r), "the camera curve's values only with it on");
+    r.camera = true;
+    check(field("grade.camera_gamma")->relevant(r) && field("grade.camera_knee")->relevant(r), "the camera curve's values");
+    check(!field("game.barrel")->relevant(r), "the game's barrel is one of the game's own settings");
+    r.game_look = true;
+    check(field("game.barrel")->relevant(r), "the game's barrel with the game's look on");
+    // Not finite comes back as the default.
+    Settings bad;
+    bad.zoom = std::nanf("");
+    bad.fov = 1e9f;
+    const auto fixed = clamped(bad);
+    check(fixed.zoom == 1.0f && fixed.fov == 170.0f, "clamped: not finite is the default, too big is the top");
+}
